screens.prose:
To save a file, someone puts a body in `returns.h`. Both `main.cpp` and `pricer.cpp` include it.

```cpp
// returns.h
#pragma once
double simple_return(double before, double after) {
    return (after - before) / before;
}
```

The pattern you used:

```cpp
// returns.h: declarations, defaults, #pragma once
double annualise(double daily_vol, int days = 252);
// returns.cpp: one body each
double annualise(double daily_vol, int days) { ... }
// main.cpp: include, then call
#include "returns.h"
```

Build with `g++ -std=c++17 main.cpp returns.cpp -o backtest`.

quiz.prose:
Two functions share a name: an **overload**. The compiler picks one by the argument types.

```cpp
double mid(double bid, double ask) { return (bid + ask) / 2; }
long long mid(long long bid, long long ask) { return (bid + ask) / 2; }

std::cout << mid(10001LL, 10002LL) << ' ' << mid(100.01, 100.02);
```
